      "message": "fix(dxf): MPOLYGON and the 3D surface kinds count as entities in the inert-section scan\n\nENTITY_KINDS lacked MPOLYGON and the six SURFACE subtypes (EXTRUDEDSURFACE,\nLOFTEDSURFACE, NURBSURFACE, PLANESURFACE, REVOLVEDSURFACE, SWEPTSURFACE), so a\ndamaged file could hide one of them in CLASSES, ACDSDATA or THUMBNAILIMAGE and\nthe reader dropped it silently. They are refused now, like the other kinds.\n\nSUN stays off the list on purpose: AutoCAD writes it in OBJECTS (AcDbSun, no\nAcDbEntity), and OBJECTS refuses every listed kind. A comment says why and a\ntest pins that a SUN object in OBJECTS still imports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nFixes #3683",
